==English==
[[Image:Canon A-1.jpg|thumb|right|A camera.]]
[[File:Radcliffe Camera, Oxford - Oct 2006.jpg|thumb|Radcliffe Camera, Oxford]]

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:lbor|la:camera}}
{{lbor|en|la|camera|t=chamber or bedchamber}}, from {{der|en|grc|καμάρα|t=anything with an arched cover, a covered carriage or boat, a vaulted chamber, a vault}}, of {{der|en|ira-old|-}} origin, from {{der|en|ira-pro|*kamarā-|t=something curved}}, from {{m|ira-pro|*kamárati}}, from {{der|en|iir-pro|*kmárati}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kh₂em-||to bend, curve}}. {{dbt|en|chamber}}.

{{sense|device}} An {{ellipsis|en|camera obscura|nocap=1}}, from {{der|en|la-new|camera obscura|t=dark chamber}}, because the first cameras used a [[pinhole]] and a dark room.

